{"slug":"elements","number":"7","title":"Measures of elements and clearance envelopes","file":"spec/rules/07-elements.md","sections":[{"id":"7.1","number":"7.1","title":"Members"},{"id":"7.2","number":"7.2","title":"The room an element is in"},{"id":"7.3","number":"7.3","title":"Heights above the floor"},{"id":"7.4","number":"7.4","title":"Protection"},{"id":"7.5","number":"7.5","title":"Envelopes as declared"},{"id":"7.6","number":"7.6","title":"Obstructions"},{"id":"7.7","number":"7.7","title":"Clear depth in front"},{"id":"7.8","number":"7.8","title":"Overlapping envelopes"}],"blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["The measures of ",{"t":"a","href":"#7.1","c":["7.1"]}," to ",{"t":"a","href":"#7.4","c":["7.4"]}," take an extension element as their target; those of ",{"t":"a","href":"#7.5","c":["7.5"]}," to ",{"t":"a","href":"#7.8","c":["7.8"]}," take a clearance envelope. An element's fallback, placement and clearance envelopes are Core's (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/extensions#12.6","c":["12.6"]},", §13.4, §13.5); its frame is Core's (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/hosting#13.1","c":["13.1"]},")."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"7.1","number":"7.1","c":["Members"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Measure"],["Arguments"],["Type"],["Value"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"elementMember"}],[{"t":"code","v":"name"},": a member name matching ",{"t":"code","v":"^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*$"}," (required); ",{"t":"code","v":"type"},": ",{"t":"code","v":"\"integer\""},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"term\""},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"terms\""}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"boolean\""}," (required); ",{"t":"code","v":"unit"},": ",{"t":"code","v":"\"V\""},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"A\""}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"W\""}," (optional, with ",{"t":"code","v":"\"type\": \"integer\""}," only)"],["as ",{"t":"code","v":"type"}],["the element's member ",{"t":"code","v":"name"},", read with its default (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/0.1/measures#4.5","c":["4.5"]},"), when it is of ",{"t":"code","v":"type"}," — a JSON integer, a string, an array of strings, or a boolean; otherwise no value"]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"elementMember"}," reads the element's extension (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/0.1/measures#4.6","c":["4.6"]},") — the extension the rule names for its targets (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/0.1/rules#3.9","c":["3.9"]},"): a receptacle's ",{"t":"code","v":"amps"},", an alarm's ",{"t":"code","v":"detects"},", a water heater's ",{"t":"code","v":"energy"},". An integer with a ",{"t":"code","v":"unit"}," is displayed with it (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/0.1/findings#9.6","c":["9.6"]},"). A member the element does not have, and its extension gives no default, has no value (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/0.1/measures#4.2","c":["4.2"]},"); so does one of another type than ",{"t":"code","v":"type"},"."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-7.1.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST compute ",{"t":"code","v":"elementMember"}," as this section defines it."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"7.2","number":"7.2","c":["The room an element is in"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Measure"],["Arguments"],["Type"],["Value"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"elementRoomFunction"}],["—"],["term"],["the ",{"t":"code","v":"roomFunction"}," (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/0.1/rooms#5.1","c":["5.1"]},") of the room the element is in (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/0.1/measures#4.4","c":["4.4"]},"), or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"none\""}," when it is in no room"]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-7.2.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST compute ",{"t":"code","v":"elementRoomFunction"}," as this section defines it."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"7.3","number":"7.3","c":["Heights above the floor"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Measure"],["Arguments"],["Type"],["Value"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"elementBottomAboveFloor"}],["—"],["length"],["the bottom of its fallback (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/extensions#12.6","c":["12.6"]},") above the floor of its level (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/rules/0.1/measures#4.1","c":["4.1"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"elementTopAboveFloor"}],["—"],["length"],["the top of its fallback above the floor of its level"]]]},{"t":"p","c":["A panel's highest breaker, a water heater's burner, a receptacle's centre: a fallback box is the element's extent, so a rule about a height reads the box an extension's writer gives the element."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-7.3.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST compute the measures of this section as this section defines them."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"7.4","number":"7.4","c":["Protection"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Measure"],["Arguments"],["Type"],["Value"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"elementProtectedBy"}],[{"t":"code","v":"protection"},": ",{"t":"code","v":"\"gfci\""}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"afci\""}," (required)"],["boolean"],["whether the element has ",{"t":"code","v":"protection"}," in its own ",{"t":"code","v":"features"}," (FS_electrical §2.2), read with its default, or is a load (FS_electrical §3.2) of a circuit that has ",{"t":"code","v":"protection"}," in its ",{"t":"code","v":"protection"}]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"elementProtectedBy"}," reads FS_electrical. Its result's ",{"t":"code","v":"involved"}," lists the circuits that give the protection."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-7.4.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST compute ",{"t":"code","v":"elementProtectedBy"}," as this section defines it."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"7.5","number":"7.5","c":["Envelopes as declared"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Measure"],["Arguments"],["Type"],["Value"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"envelopePurpose"}],["—"],["term"],["its ",{"t":"code","v":"purpose"},": ",{"t":"code","v":"\"workingSpace\""},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"fixtureClearance\""},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"swing\""}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"access\""}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"envelopeDepth"}],["—"],["length"],[{"t":"code","v":"max.x − min.x"},": how far it reaches forward"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"envelopeWidth"}],["—"],["length"],[{"t":"code","v":"max.y − min.y"}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"envelopeHeight"}],["—"],["length"],[{"t":"code","v":"max.z − min.z"}]],[[{"t":"code","v":"envelopeBottomAboveFloor"}],["—"],["length"],["its bottom (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/hosting#13.2","c":["13.2"]},") above the floor of its owner's level"]]]},{"t":"p","c":["These read the envelope as its owner declares it. Whether the space it names is actually clear is ",{"t":"a","href":"#7.6","c":["7.6"]}," to ",{"t":"a","href":"#7.8","c":["7.8"]},"."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-7.5.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST compute the measures of this section as this section defines them."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"7.6","number":"7.6","c":["Obstructions"]},{"t":"p","c":["An envelope ",{"t":"code","v":"E"},", of owner ",{"t":"code","v":"X"}," on level ",{"t":"code","v":"L"},", is the box ",{"t":"code","v":"[x0, x1] × [y0, y1] × [z0, z1]"}," in ",{"t":"code","v":"X"},"'s frame (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/hosting#13.5","c":["13.5"]},"). Its ",{"t":"strong","c":["plan rectangle"]}," is the set of plan points whose local coordinates ",{"t":"code","v":"(p, q)"}," (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/hosting#13.1","c":["13.1"]},") have ",{"t":"code","v":"x0 ≤ p ≤ x1"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"y0 ≤ q ≤ y1"}," — exactly, not rounded — and its vertical range is ",{"t":"code","v":"[bottom, top]"},", its derived bottom and top (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/hosting#13.2","c":["13.2"]},")."]},{"t":"p","c":["Its ",{"t":"strong","c":["obstacles"]}," are:"]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","c":["every wall on ",{"t":"code","v":"L"},", except the wall that hosts ",{"t":"code","v":"X"}," (an opening's wall, or a ",{"t":"code","v":"wallFace"}," host's wall): the wall's outline (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/walls#5.7","c":["5.7"]},"), from its base elevation to its top elevation (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/walls#5.9","c":["5.9"]},");"]}],[{"t":"p","c":["every extension element other than ",{"t":"code","v":"X"}," whose fallback's ",{"t":"code","v":"level"}," is ",{"t":"code","v":"L"},": its fallback's footprint (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/extensions#12.6","c":["12.6"]},"), from its bottom to its top."]}]]},{"t":"p","c":["An obstacle ",{"t":"strong","c":["obstructs"]}," ",{"t":"code","v":"E"}," when the interior of its plan polygon and the interior of ",{"t":"code","v":"E"},"'s plan rectangle intersect, and its vertical range and ",{"t":"code","v":"E"},"'s overlap by a positive length. An opening does not open a wall here: a wall with a door in it obstructs the space in front of a panel as the wall would without one."]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Measure"],["Arguments"],["Type"],["Value"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"envelopeObstructions"}],["—"],["count"],["the number of ",{"t":"code","v":"E"},"'s obstacles that obstruct it; ",{"t":"code","v":"involved"}," lists them"]]]},{"t":"p","c":["A boiler set beside a panel, inside the panel's working space, obstructs it; so does the wall of a closet too shallow for the space. A door's swing over the working space is not an obstruction but an overlap of envelopes (",{"t":"a","href":"#7.8","c":["7.8"]},")."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-7.6.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST compute ",{"t":"code","v":"envelopeObstructions"}," as this section defines it."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"7.7","number":"7.7","c":["Clear depth in front"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Measure"],["Arguments"],["Type"],["Value"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"clearDepthInFront"}],[{"t":"code","v":"limit"},": a length greater than zero (required)"],["length"],["how far forward from ",{"t":"code","v":"E"},"'s near face the space stays clear, within ",{"t":"code","v":"E"},"'s width and height, up to ",{"t":"code","v":"limit"}]]]},{"t":"p","c":["The ",{"t":"strong","c":["strip"]}," in front of ",{"t":"code","v":"E"}," is the set of plan points whose local coordinates have ",{"t":"code","v":"p > x0"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"y0 < q < y1"},". For each obstacle of ",{"t":"code","v":"E"}," (",{"t":"a","href":"#7.6","c":["7.6"]},") whose vertical range overlaps ",{"t":"code","v":"E"},"'s by a positive length, and whose plan polygon's interior meets the strip, its ",{"t":"strong","c":["distance"]}," is the greatest lower bound of ",{"t":"code","v":"p − x0"}," over the points of its interior in the strip. The clear depth ",{"t":"code","v":"D"}," is the least of these distances, or unbounded when there is none; the measure is ",{"t":"code","v":"min(limit, round(D))"},". Its ",{"t":"code","v":"involved"}," lists the obstacles whose distance is exactly ",{"t":"code","v":"D"},", when ",{"t":"code","v":"round(D)"}," is less than ",{"t":"code","v":"limit"},", and is empty otherwise."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"code","v":"clearDepthInFront"}," measures past the envelope's own depth, up to ",{"t":"code","v":"limit"},": a rule that asks for three feet of clear space in front of a panel reads ",{"t":"code","v":"clearDepthInFront"}," with a limit of three feet, whatever depth the panel's writer declared. The search runs within the envelope's width and height, so a wall above the envelope's top, or beside it, does not shorten it."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-7.7.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST compute ",{"t":"code","v":"clearDepthInFront"}," as this section defines it."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"7.8","number":"7.8","c":["Overlapping envelopes"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"head":[["Measure"],["Arguments"],["Type"],["Value"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"envelopeOverlaps"}],[{"t":"code","v":"purpose"},": a purpose (optional)"],["count"],["the number of envelopes of other owners that overlap ",{"t":"code","v":"E"}," (Core §",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/0.3/hosting#13.6","c":["13.6"]},") — of that purpose, when given; ",{"t":"code","v":"involved"}," lists their owners"]]]},{"t":"p","c":["This is Core's overlap measure, read as Core derives it: a door's ",{"t":"code","v":"swing"}," over a panel's ",{"t":"code","v":"workingSpace"}," is one overlap of each."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-RULES-7.8.1","level":"MUST","c":["An evaluator MUST compute ",{"t":"code","v":"envelopeOverlaps"}," as this section defines it."]}]}]}
